Problem
We need to merge two sorted linked lists into one sorted list.
 
Approach
I compare the current nodes of both lists and add the smaller node to the result. I continue until one list becomes empty, then I add the remaining nodes.

Time Complexity
Time Complexity: O(n + m)
Each node from both lists is checked only once.
Space Complexity: O(1)
I only use pointers and reuse the existing nodes.

Reflection / Improvement
There is no faster approach because we need to check the nodes from both lists. The current solution already has optimal time and space complexity.
